{"title":"Divisibility rules/Rule 1 for 7 proof","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules/Rule_1_for_7_proof&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This is based on <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules/Rule_for_11_proof\" title=\"Divisibility rules/Rule for 11 proof\"> divisibility by 11 rule </a></i>\n</p><p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6582d1a31d1fd6bdab19f0d332c8d93adb9c66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> digits, otherwise add zeros to the left.\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\"> WLOG </a> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e753caa85cb6565afb12e08a24b8d780e175e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = a_{3k-1}a_{3k-2}a_{3k-3}\\cdots a_8a_7a_6a_5a_4a_3a_2a_1a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"348\" height=\"18\" /> where the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base_numbers\" title=\"Base numbers\"> base-ten</a> numbers. \nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/9469da81b9dce0e2ee479ed5eba185d53c25ce98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N = 10^{3k-1} a_{3k-1} + 10^{3k-2} a_{3k-2} + 10^{3k-3} a_{3k-3} \\cdots + 10^8 a_8 + 10^7 a_7 + 10^6 a_6 + 10^5 a_5 + 10^4 a_4 + 10^3 a_3 + 10^2 a_2 + 10 a_1 + a_0\\]\" width=\"843\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cbeb3bbab48c42ba019a24ac0e0211b9e93f9a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 1000^{k-1} (100 a_{3k-1} + 10 a_{3k-2} + a_{3k-3}) \\cdots + 1000^2 (100 a_8 + 10 a_7 + a_6) + 1000 (100 a_5 + 10 a_4 + a_3) + (100 a_2 + 10 a_1 + a_0).\\]\" width=\"859\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Rewriting or partitioning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> into 3 digit numbers (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf7b7175fba3442d3f6735d1811c22c94ea94745.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3k-1}a_{3k-2}a_{3k-3}\\cdots a_8a_7a_6 a_5a_4a_3 a_2a_1a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"307\" height=\"14\" />).\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abfa50d0aca61b16cea3ea5ad1478cf1e58bc3a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 1000^{k-1} (a_{3k-1}a_{3k-2}a_{3k-3}) \\cdots + 1000^2 (a_8a_7a_6) + 1000 (a_5a_4a_3) + (a_2a_1a_0).\\\\ \\equiv (-1)^{k-1} (a_{3k-1}a_{3k-2}a_{3k-3}) \\cdots + (-1)^2 (a_8a_7a_6) - (a_5a_4a_3) + (a_2a_1a_0) \\pmod {7}, \\text{since} 1000\\equiv -1\\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThis is the alternating sum of groups of 3 digit numbers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, which is what we wanted.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules/Rule_1_for_7_proof&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility_rules\" title=\"Divisibility rules\"> Back to divisibility rules</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082944\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 58/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2336/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25895:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082944 and revision id 228812. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}